y music», derivada del último Cabaret Voltaire con influencia disco y de ciencia ficción: Geography de Front 242 es el disco hito; después Klinik, Neon Judgement, Vomito Negro. En Vancouver, Skinny Puppy y Front Line Assembly, profetas de la generación cyberpunk. Los cimientos de la música de baile alternativa de los noventa.","color":"#94a3b8","family":"Gótico e industrial","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#ebm"},{"id":121512346364895,"name":"Cut’n’paste","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1983,"end":1991,"desc":"El sampler y el tocadiscos como instrumento generador: música construida como un collage cortando y pegando fuentes diversas.","color":"#f87171","family":"Hip hop, breaks y ritmo lento","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#cut-n-paste"},{"id":113621567253534,"name":"Darkcore","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1990,"end":1993,"desc":"Desviación oscura del hardcore británico: breaks hiperacelerados y efectos violentos. Semilla del drum’n’bass.","color":"#4ade80","family":"Rave y continuum hardcore","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#darkcore"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":190750918785636,"artist":"Meat Beat Manifesto","artist_id":195943444961625,"title":"Storm The Studio","year":1989,"ess":0,"yt":"7KrK0mV6TNE","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Electronic Body Music","scene_id":61612725722255,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#ebm","chapters":["Sección 5.18"],"pages":[[1,199,null]]},{"id":118235793732840,"artist":"Meat Beat Manifesto","artist_id":195943444961625,"title":"Radio Babylon","year":1990,"ess":0,"yt":"ak169_XCiXs","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Darkcore","scene_id":113621567253534,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#darkcore","chapters":["Cap. 15: Progresión lógica: jungle, drum’n’bass y 2step (1990-2002)"],"pages":[[1,275]]},{"id":34731272729553,"artist":"Meat Beat Manifesto","artist_id":195943444961625,"title":"Actual Sounds And Voices","year":1998,"ess":0,"yt":"FgHnqrl3Q44","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Electronic Body Music","scene_id":61612725722255,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#ebm","chapters":["Sección 5.18"],"pages":[[1,199,null]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":199,"text":"…in the early 1980s, and the likes of Front 242 and Skinny Puppy had made a career of crossing over into \"Electronic Body Music\" (EBM). Jack Dangers' Meat Beat Manifesto (2) were one of the most creative bands of the industrial-dance crossover. Their Storm The Studio (1989), offering a thick mix of hyper-cinetic…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":292,"text":"…power to the electronic beat. The result was a syncopated variant of house, a fusion of hip hop and techno. The style had been predated by Meat Beat Manifesto in 1990 and was adopted at the London club \"Rage\" by disc-jockeys Fabio and Grooverider. The \"inventors\" were Roni Size , LTJ Bukem, 4 Hero (and…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":326,"text":"…Sin, Flaming Lips's Telepathic Surgery, Bitch Magnet's Umber, Dogbowl's Tit, Godflesh's Streetcleaner ？ Paradise Lost invents \"doom-metal\" ？ Meat Beat Manifesto invents \"jungle\" (or \"drum'n'bass\") music, a syncopated variant of house, a fusion of hip hop and techno, that is adopted at the London club \"Rage\"…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"